From 630fd794c444f69aab12a4885d98e922974c0229 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.net>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 20:20:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] stdio: scanf keeps its look-ahead character on a pipe

scanf's file reader returned each character and then fseek'ed back to
it, so the character scanf stops at stayed in the stream. On a pipe
fseek drops the FILE's read buffer and fails: the look-ahead character
and all input already buffered were lost, and every later read on the
stream returned EOF.

Put each character back into the FILE's unget buffer instead (as
ungetc does) and take it out when the next character is read. The
stream ends where it did before on a file, and now also on a pipe.
Test stdio/fscanf_pipe, its expected output from glibc.
---
